 ## Overview
-Voxel Visibility Culling determines which voxels in a volume dataset are perceptually relevant to the viewer, allowing the renderer to skip processing occluded or low-importance regions [S1][S2, S3, S4, S5, S6, unofficial]. It solves the problem of rendering unnecessary data by filtering voxels based on geometric position, structural coherence, or feature importance [S1][S2, S3, S4, S5, S6, unofficial]. It differs from its sibling [Voxel Occupancy Test](1281-voxel-occupancy-test.md) by not merely checking if a voxel is occupied, but evaluating its visibility relative to a camera or structural context [S1][S2, S3, S4, S5, S6, unofficial]. It differs from [Near Plane Visibility Culling](10816-near-plane-visibility-culling.md) by handling broader visibility criteria (such as gradient-based importance) rather than just near-plane clipping, and from [Obstacle-Flag](14294-obstacle-flag.md) by being a static pre-calculation or metric rather than a dynamic scheduling state [S1][S2, S3, S4, S5, S6, unofficial].
